From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: keep the host up if the link fails on resume

dw_pcie_resume_noirq() tears the host down when the link times out and
leaves pci->suspended set. By the code, the PM core goes on to resume the
Root Port and its children anyway, and they reach the controller through
the DBI with its clocks off, and on Qualcomm with the CPU-PCIe path off as
well. The
next suspend does the same in dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() and disables
everything a second time. So one link that fails to train can take the
whole SoC down. This comes from reading the code, it hasn't been seen on
hardware.

Only -ETIMEDOUT takes this path, -ENODEV and -EIO keep the host up. Keep it
up for -ETIMEDOUT too. By the code, the Root Port then stays accessible,
config accesses to its children fail at the link check in
dw_pcie_other_conf_map_bus(), and the next suspend starts with the host up.
BAR accesses to the children aren't guarded, the same as after the other
two errors. The -ETIMEDOUT case hasn't been seen on hardware either.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
index 06722259d..30adfa657 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -1313,9 +1313,14 @@ int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_deinit;
 
-	ret = dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
-	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
-		goto err_stop_link;
+	/*
+	 * The PM core resumes the Root Port and its children whatever happens
+	 * here, and they reach the controller through the DBI. Keep the host
+	 * up if the link failed: config accesses to the children fail at the
+	 * link check in dw_pcie_other_conf_map_bus(), while tearing the host
+	 * down would leave the DBI unclocked.
+	 */
+	dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
 
 	if (pci->pp.ops->post_init)
 		pci->pp.ops->post_init(&pci->pp);
@@ -1324,9 +1329,6 @@ int dw_pcie_resume_noirq(struct dw_pcie *pci)
 
 	return 0;
 
-err_stop_link:
-	dw_pcie_stop_link(pci);
-
 err_deinit:
 	if (pci->pp.ops->deinit)
 		pci->pp.ops->deinit(&pci->pp);
